// Asymmetric Line coverage — Rg/Xg/Kxg ground-return frequency correction.
// The deck does NOT set LongLineCorrection (default FALSE, Circuit.pas:492), so
// YPrim is assembled by the NON-LLC else branch (Line.pas:1281-1287), NOT the
// sibling LongLineCorrection branch (:1262-1269). The Xgmod formula is identical
// in both (:1282 == :1263), but the ZinvValues assembly genuinely differs: the
// else branch scales the whole imaginary part by FreqMultiplier
// (:1287, `(im - Xgmod)*LenMult*FreqMult`) whereas the LLC branch scales only
// Xgmod (:1269, `(im - Xgmod*FreqMult)*LenMult`).
// SymComponentsModel lines with EXPLICIT non-default Rg/Xg/rho, solved at the
// 7th harmonic (`Set frequency=420`, FreqMultiplier=7) so the earth-return
// terms actually enter YPrim:
//   * lgx: Xg <> 0, Rg = 0 -> the `if Xg<>0` Xgmod branch fires
//     (Xgmod = 0.5*Kxg*ln(FreqMultiplier), Line.pas:1282); Rg add is 0.
//   * lgr: Rg <> 0, Xg = 0 -> Xgmod = 0; the Rg*(FreqMultiplier-1) real add
//     fires (Line.pas:1287). Clean per-term isolation.
// rho is set explicitly per line (150 / 200) to pin the
// Kxg = Xg / ln(658.5*sqrt(rho/BaseFrequency)) dependence (Line.pas:520/713/967).
//
// U1.2 INVARIANT (tracked in the upgrade ledger rows B2/D1 — this is an upgrade-
// ledger item, NOT a compat-precision shim): Kxg deliberately KEEPS the 658.5
// constant while SimpleCarson Get_Ze moves 658.5 -> 658.853. 658.5 is the
// faithful 0.14.5 spec literal at every Kxg site (Line.pas:520/713/967) and the
// newer engine keeps it there too, so it is NOT a port-introduced inexactness to
// be wiped in the precision cleanup pass — hence the Kxg code sites carry no
// compat tag (deliberately: the greppable compat-tag namespace stays a pure
// index of section-6 cleanup sites). This deck is the
// regression proving the inconsistency: its YPrim must NOT move under U1.2 (do
// NOT flip to capi015). The SymComponentsModel path never calls Get_Ze, so only
// the 658.5-in-Kxg constant is observable here.
//
// r0 <> r1 keeps the 0-sequence correction distinct. Linear per-phase-unequal
// shunt reactors draw the unbalanced current (autotrans_gic set-frequency-
// snapshot pattern; no nonlinear loads -> frequency-well-defined on both
// engines). Line YPrims compared directly.
Clear
Set DefaultBaseFrequency=60

New Circuit.line_ground_z_asym basekv=115 pu=1.0 angle=0 phases=3 bus1=src
~ mvasc3=20000 mvasc1=21000

! Xg-only line: Xgmod branch active, Rg add zeroed.
New Line.lgx bus1=src bus2=b1 phases=3 r1=0.06 x1=0.55 r0=0.20 x0=1.60 c1=3.2 c0=1.5 Rg=0 Xg=0.30 rho=150 length=40 units=mi

! Rg-only line: Rg*(FreqMultiplier-1) add active, Xgmod zeroed.
New Line.lgr bus1=b1 bus2=b2 phases=3 r1=0.08 x1=0.60 r0=0.24 x0=1.75 c1=3.0 c0=1.4 Rg=0.12 Xg=0 rho=200 length=35 units=mi

! Per-phase-unequal shunt reactors -> unbalanced current at the harmonic.
New Reactor.rb1a phases=1 bus1=b1.1 r=2.0 x=140
New Reactor.rb1b phases=1 bus1=b1.2 r=2.0 x=210
New Reactor.rb1c phases=1 bus1=b1.3 r=2.0 x=175
New Reactor.rb2a phases=1 bus1=b2.1 r=2.0 x=160
New Reactor.rb2c phases=1 bus1=b2.3 r=2.0 x=195

Set voltagebases=[115]
calcv
Set frequency=420
Solve
